    "body": "**Update:** I did proper research and wrote about it on [Discord](https://discord.com/channels/567163873606500352/567163873606500354/835246328514347078):\r\n> Seems like emoji made using variant selector `\\u{fe0f}` require double space after them to prevent possible rendering glitches due to miscalculated width\r\n\r\nAccording to quick [regex search](https://sourcegraph.com/search?q=repo:%5Egithub%5C.com/starship/starship%24+symbol:+%22%5CS*%5Cx%7Bfe0f%7D&patternType=regexp) modules that require double space after symbol are:\r\n- SHLVL\r\n- AWS\r\n- GCloud\r\n- OpenStack\r\n- Nix\r\n\r\nI guess that makes this a non-issue? I mean it does look weird but it is an intentional _safety_ measure :shrug: ",
