    "created_at": "2021-04-29T16:39:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-29T16:42:17Z",
    "body": "> Seems like emoji made using variant selector `\\u{fe0f}` require double space after them to prevent possible rendering glitches due to miscalculated width\n\nEven though I'm aware of the variant selector (and the issues it may cause, such as neovim/neovim#7151), that's still good to know!\n\n> I guess that makes this a non-issue? I mean it does look weird but it is an intentional _safety_ measure :shrug: \n\nRight. The extra space may be needed in some terminals/configs, and it can be easily redefined.\n\nHope other people having the same question will see this issue 😄",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
